[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2779578161","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105021#issuecomment-2779578161","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105021","id":2779578161,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6lrP8x","user":{"login":"precup","id":709680,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwOTY4MA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/709680?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup","html_url":"https://github.com/precup","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-04T19:29:30Z","updated_at":"2025-04-04T19:29:30Z","body":"Could you at least cut down your project to the scenes involved and upload it as a zip, even if you can't repro it in a new project? It would be very helpful to have a repro project. The exact error messages would also be helpful.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2779578161/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2779759454","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105021#issuecomment-2779759454","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105021","id":2779759454,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6lr8Ne","user":{"login":"betalars","id":18014034,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDE0MDM0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18014034?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars","html_url":"https://github.com/betalars","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-04T21:27:12Z","updated_at":"2025-04-04T21:27:12Z","body":"> Could you at least cut down your project to the scenes involved and upload it as a zip, even if you can't repro it in a new project? It would be very helpful to have a repro project. The exact error messages would also be helpful.\n\nOkay first of all: here are the exact error Messages:\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d5c190ce-225e-4715-abbd-15503aee0545)\n\nI have tried just including the related files in a demo project, but I kept getting different errors so either you have to swallow the pill and download my entire game or I need to find the time to keep gutting my project until only this error is left.\n\nBTW: i changed the script so it dynamically loads the extra stuff i put in Scene B so I can just use Scene A for everything and that seems to be a workaround.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2779759454/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2779765563","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105021#issuecomment-2779765563","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105021","id":2779765563,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6lr9s7","user":{"login":"betalars","id":18014034,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDE0MDM0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18014034?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars","html_url":"https://github.com/betalars","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-04T21:31:48Z","updated_at":"2025-04-04T21:31:48Z","body":"Oh and @precup sorry I forgot to include a link to the repo in my original post ... you unfortunately need to use the Godot-Steam build or disable a few Lines. Will get to creating a better MRP soonisch.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2779765563/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3243178483","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105021#issuecomment-3243178483","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105021","id":3243178483,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7BTvnz","user":{"login":"advance2112","id":90730477,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNzMwNDc3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90730477?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/advance2112","html_url":"https://github.com/advance2112","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/advance2112/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/advance2112/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/advance2112/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/advance2112/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/advance2112/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/advance2112/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/advance2112/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/advance2112/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/advance2112/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-01T19:58:11Z","updated_at":"2025-09-01T20:05:29Z","body":"Ran into this issue when working on [this game](https://quencheddisorder.itch.io/the-gnaw-protocol). This was an issue with the enemies within the game, which similar to what was described in the OP, were saved in a number of different scenes that all used the same script. The workaround was to create a bunch of change-nothing extensions of the main script, one for each scene.\n\nThe issue was bugging me though, and seemed elusive, so I messed around with it a bit and managed to make an MRP:\n\n[GodotIssue105021MRP.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/22083490/GodotIssue105021MRP.zip)\n\nYou'll notice that you consistently get this error when loading main.tscn:\n```\nE 0:00:00:761   _printerr: res://Scenes/spinner2.tscn:7 - Parse Error: [ext_resource] referenced non-existent resource at: res://Scripts/spinner.gd.\n  <C++ Source>  scene/resources/resource_format_text.cpp:39 @ _printerr()\n```\nand the spinner on the left (spinner1.tscn) works, while the spinner on the right (spinner2.tscn) does not spin, since its script failed to load.\n\nWhat's curious is that if you do any of the following things, the error goes away and the script loads correctly:\n* comment out line 6 in spinner.gd: `DoNothing.do_nothing()`\n* comment out line 4 in do_nothing.gd: `var nothing = Global2.NOTHING`\n* comment out lines 5 and 6 in global2.gd: `const SPINNER_1 = Global1.SPINNER_1...`\n* change lines 5 and 6 in global2.gd to `const SPINNER_1 = preload(\"res://Scenes/spinner1.tscn\")...`\n\nClearly this is more complex than just having the same script on multiple scenes, and has something to do with Globals and possibly how preload() works. I am not well versed enough to speculate any further than that, but I hope the MRP is useful for debugging this.\n\nEdit 1: Forgot to mention: this was performed on Windows 11, Godot 4.4.1","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3243178483/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3460296792","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105021#issuecomment-3460296792","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105021","id":3460296792,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7OP_BY","user":{"login":"MadeScientist","id":190612698,"node_id":"U_kgDOC1yE2g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/190612698?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist","html_url":"https://github.com/MadeScientist","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-29T08:11:49Z","updated_at":"2025-10-29T08:43:48Z","body":"I encountered the same problem in 4.5.1. I will open a separate issue when i back home. The issue can be stably reproduced.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3460296792/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3477955912","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105021#issuecomment-3477955912","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105021","id":3477955912,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7PTWVI","user":{"login":"xuhuisheng","id":1118508,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMTg1MDg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1118508?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng","html_url":"https://github.com/xuhuisheng","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-02T13:17:05Z","updated_at":"2025-11-02T13:17:05Z","body":"Looks like `[GodotIssue105021MRP.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/22083490/GodotIssue105021MRP.zip)` has circular reference.\n\n- `spinner2.tscn` references `spinner.gd`\n- `spinner.gd` references `do_nothing.gd`\n-  `do_nothing.gd` references `global2.gd`\n- `global2.gd` referenes `global1.gd`\n- `global1.gd` references `spinner2.tscn`","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3477955912/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4351571469","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105021#issuecomment-4351571469","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105021","id":4351571469,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABA1-2DQ","user":{"login":"malciin","id":23403545,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzNDAzNTQ1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23403545?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/malciin","html_url":"https://github.com/malciin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/malciin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/malciin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/malciin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/malciin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/malciin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/malciin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/malciin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/malciin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/malciin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-30T10:11:31Z","updated_at":"2026-04-30T10:11:38Z","body":"I can confirm - that error is related to circular dependency - I ran into the same issue in a scenario where the user can navigate between Scene A and Scene B (in both directions). At first, I tried wiring the scenes in the editor using a shared helper script like:\n`button_change_scene.gd`\n\n```gdscript\nextends Button\n\n@export var scene: PackedScene\n\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n    pressed.connect(_on_pressed)\n\nfunc _on_pressed() -> void:\n    get_tree().change_scene_to_packed(scene)\n\n```\n\nUnfortunately, for now, I had to fall back to using raw string paths to connect these scenes to avoid circular reference.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4351571469/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5805466779","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105021#issuecomment-5805466779","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105021","id":5805466779,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABWghkmw","user":{"login":"Solesaver","id":3838015,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4MzgwMTU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3838015?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Solesaver","html_url":"https://github.com/Solesaver","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Solesaver/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Solesaver/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Solesaver/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Solesaver/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Solesaver/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Solesaver/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Solesaver/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Solesaver/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Solesaver/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-24T00:51:43Z","updated_at":"2026-09-24T00:51:43Z","body":"Hit this issue. Made my own MRP.\n[shared-script-issue.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/32587584/shared-script-issue.zip)\n\nIt's a combination of the circular dependency and the shared script. As you can see in my blink.gd.\n```\n\tif parent is Player:\n\t\tpass\n```\nIs fine even though it's the exact same circular dependency as the next block.\n```\n\t#if parent is Enemy:\n\t\t#pass\n```\nIf you uncomment that bit, the enemy breaks.\n\nSome additional background, I set up 'Player' first for this project, then added 'Enemy'. When I was trying to hone in why I could reference 'Player' but not 'Enemy', I set up third 'Player_2' object. When I had 'Player_2' and 'Enemy' in the same scene it was 'Enemy' that was ok to reference in blink.gd, but referencing the 'Player_2' class_name caused the 'Player_2' blinker to break. I cleaned all of that up to keep this \"MRP\" minimal, but thought it was worth noting.\n\nGodot Engine 4.7.2.stable.steam\nWindows 11 Pro","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5805466779/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5819541903","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105021#issuecomment-5819541903","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105021","id":5819541903,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABWt8pjw","user":{"login":"Solesaver","id":3838015,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4MzgwMTU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3838015?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Solesaver","html_url":"https://github.com/Solesaver","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Solesaver/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Solesaver/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Solesaver/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Solesaver/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Solesaver/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Solesaver/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Solesaver/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Solesaver/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Solesaver/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-24T18:10:03Z","updated_at":"2026-09-24T18:12:48Z","body":"Quick follow-up to show how I worked around the issue in my own project, here's a minimal edit to my MRP that works around the issue.\n[shared-script-issue-workaround.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/32621162/shared-script-issue-workaround.zip)\n\nInstead of using `@onready` and preload, I changed it to use `@export`:\n```\nclass_name Player\nextends Node2D\n\n@export var blink_scene: PackedScene = null\n#@onready var blink_scene: PackedScene = preload(\"res://player_blink.tscn\")\n```\nand\n```\nclass_name Enemy\nextends Node2D\n\n@export var blink_scene: PackedScene = null\n#@onready var blink_scene: PackedScene = preload(\"res://enemy_blink.tscn\")\n```\nThis allows me to safely uncomment the reference to Enemy in blink.gd:\n```\n\tif parent is Player:\n\t\tpass\n\tif parent is Enemy:\n\t\tpass\n```\n\nGiven that preload and passing the PackedScene in as an export variable should be functionally identical, it seems like the extra step of resolving the export variable provides just enough leeway to break the detected circular dependency or the circular dependency detection in the preload code path is just unnecessarily aggressive.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5819541903/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]